  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "canon",
      "title": "Tenet (2020), theatrical cut",
      "kind": "canon_statement",
      "text": "Turnstiles invert a traveller's time direction. The Protagonist recruits Neil; they run a temporal pincer on Stalsk-12 (red team forward, blue team inverted, 10-minute offset). Neil is revealed as the soldier who died saving the Protagonist at the Kyiv opera - an inverted strand from the future. The Algorithm is assembled and hidden in the past."
    },
    {
      "id": "allocation",
      "title": "Fixture allocations",
      "kind": "test_fixture",
      "text": "Inverted passage is modelled as a transfer with mechanism time_travel between lane Forward and lane Inverted; the same body exists twice during overlap windows (temporal pincer). Boundary double-count (E257) is a KNOWN OPEN ISSUE - both exit and entry are charted as separate events here."
    }
